## Outward Search v2 — Architecture

### Two-Phase Execution Model
- **Phase 1: Internal DB** — Always runs, no quota cost, no adapter dispatch. Uses `InternalDbAdapter` directly.
- **Phase 2: Outward Sources** — Gated by entitlement + quota + global cap. Only registered adapters in ADAPTERS map.

Internal DB is NOT an adapter in the outward registry. It runs before adapter dispatch.

### Badge Matching — Strict (No Substring)
- `badgeMatchesVariant()` uses token-boundary regex, NOT `.includes()`
- "SR5" matches "SR5", "SR5+" but NOT "SR50"
- "GX" matches "GX" but NOT "GXL"
- Priority: 1) exact variant_family, 2) token-boundary on raw/used variants

### Cache Key — Tier-Aware
Cache key includes: intent fields + plan_tier + sorted source keys. Prevents cross-tier cache pollution.

### Global System Cap
- 300 outward searches/day across all accounts (configurable via GLOBAL_DAILY_LIMIT)
- Counts completed non-cached outward_search_runs
- Operator/cron still bypass per-account quota but counted in global

### Deduplication
- `deduplicateResults()` merges across sources using composite key: year + title prefix + km-band (5k) + price-band (500) + state
- Higher-scoring duplicate wins

### Foundation Tables
- `source_registry` — evolved with tier/adapter/health columns
- `dealer_entitlements` — per-account quota with daily reset
- `outward_search_runs` — full telemetry

### Shared Modules (`_shared/outward-search/`)
- `types.ts` — interfaces + constants
- `intent-parser.ts` — LLM + regex fallback
- `quota.ts` — checkQuota, incrementUsage, checkGlobalCap
- `adapters/internal-db.ts` — Phase 1 adapter with strict badge matching

